Relevant codes and standards include:

Canadian Electrical Code;  
Canadian National Standard CSA-282, covering emergency power supply design;  
NFPA 20, the standard for fire pumps, which specifies minimum voltage drop requirements for fire pumps, involving fire protection systems and electrical design.

To address the voltage drop issue, the first step is to determine the actual voltage drop value in the system. There are two main methods for voltage drop calculation: manual calculation and software calculation.
